# Changelog policy

- **Do not** create, edit, or append to `CHANGELOG.md` unless the user **explicitly** asks to update the changelog (e.g. "add a changelog entry", "prepare release notes", "update CHANGELOG for 1.1.x").
- Completing features, fixes, refactors, or docs work **does not** by itself warrant a changelog update.
- Do not add an "Unreleased" section or version bump prose proactively after ordinary tasks.
- When the user **does** request a changelog update: follow [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/) style, match existing section headings (`Added`, `Fixed`, `Changed`, …), and place new release blocks **above** older versions.
- Bumping `src/pyopticfilm/_version.py` is separate; only change it when the user asks for a version or release prep.

## Contributor credits

When writing a changelog entry, credit **external** contributors where it is appropriate (merged PRs, hardware enablement, substantial patches).

- **Do not** credit the maintainer **jboneng**.
- Put credits under a `### Contributors` heading in that release block.
- Format each name as a markdown link to that person’s GitHub profile: `[@username](https://github.com/username)`.

```markdown
### Contributors

- [@TobbyTravel](https://github.com/TobbyTravel) for OpticFilm 8100 (V2) support.
```
